<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>救生艇新闻：博客——保护人类</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/</link><description></description><lastBuildDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 01:24:04 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>利用月震地震波发现月球冰</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/lunar-ice-found-using-seismic-waves-from-moonquakes</link><description>通过模拟月震振动如何更快地穿过冻土，科学家们开发了一种利用地震波来定位和测量埋藏水冰的方法，以用于未来的月球任务。 [ &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/lunar-ice-found-using-seismic-waves-from-moonquakes2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 01:24:02 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/lunar-ice-found-using-seismic-waves-from-moonquakes</guid></item><item><title>用基因编码的荧光生物传感器阐明葡萄糖代谢的时空动态</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/elucidating-the-spatiotemporal-dynamics-of-glucose-metabolism-with-genetically-encoded-fluorescent-biosensors</link><description>近年来，基因编码荧光传感器迅速发展，可以实现对葡萄糖代谢中代谢物的特异性和灵敏监测。从这个角度来看，李等人。讨论不同的生物传感器及其在了解葡萄糖代谢方面的应用。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/elucidating-the-spatiotemporal-dynamics-of-glucose-metabolism-with-genetically-encoded-fluorescent-biosensors.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 01:09:02 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/elucidating-the-spatiotemporal-dynamics-of-glucose-metabolism-with-genetically-encoded-fluorescent-biosensors</guid></item><item><title>为什么尿路感染会带来伤害——以及为什么这可能是一件好事</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/why-a-uti-hurts-and-why-that-might-be-a-good-thing</link><description>澳大利亚研究人员发现了一组以前被忽视的膀胱神经，它们有助于检测尿路感染（UTI）并触发身体的反应来清除它们，为未来膀胱疼痛治疗提供了潜在的新目标。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/why-a-uti-hurts-and-why-that-might-be-a-good-thing2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 00:54:02 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/why-a-uti-hurts-and-why-that-might-be-a-good-thing</guid></item><item><title>极性分子和聚合物桥克服了有机电子学中的两个关键限制</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/polar-molecules-and-polymer-bridges-overcome-two-key-limits-in-organic-electronics</link><description>成均馆大学纳米技术高级研究所（SAINT）、纳米工程系和半导体融合工程系的 Kang Bosoek 教授领导的研究小组开发了两种新的分子设计技术，以增强有机电子材料的导电性。一种技术在聚合物内产生更多数量的电荷载流子，而另一种技术则连接传输路径，以便电荷可以不间断地移动。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/polar-molecules-and-polymer-bridges-overcome-two-key-limits-in-organic-electronics2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 00:39:02 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/polar-molecules-and-polymer-bridges-overcome-two-key-limits-in-organic-electronics</guid></item><item><title>帕金森氏症研究确定了治疗的“机会之窗”</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/parkinsons-research-identifies-window-of-opportunity-for-treatment</link><description>研究人员研究了帕金森病中的&lt;i&gt;LRRK2&lt;/i&gt;突变。这些突变在神经元损失之前扰乱了脆弱神经元的多巴胺释放，从而确定了潜在的目标和干预时机。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/parkinsons-research-identifies-window-of-opportunity-for-treatment.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 00:24:02 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/parkinsons-research-identifies-window-of-opportunity-for-treatment</guid></item><item><title>TARDIS 如何欺骗物理定律</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/how-the-tardis-cheats-the-laws-of-physics</link><description>&lt;img src="https://politepaul.com/fd/dtDF30237DhP.xml" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 00:09:02 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/how-the-tardis-cheats-the-laws-of-physics</guid></item><item><title>大脑并不总是腐烂：科学家可能最终知道人类大脑数千年来如何避免腐烂</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/brains-dont-always-rot-scientists-may-finally-know-how-human-brains-have-evaded-decay-for-thousands-of-years</link><description>数千具人类遗骸被发现，其脑组织出乎意料地完好无损。现在，一组科学家可能终于找到了原因。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/brains-dont-always-rot-scientists-may-finally-know-how-human-brains-have-evaded-decay-for-thousands-of-years2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 23:54:02 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/brains-dont-always-rot-scientists-may-finally-know-how-human-brains-have-evaded-decay-for-thousands-of-years</guid></item><item><title>科学家揭示量子流体的隐藏结构</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/scientists-reveal-hidden-structure-of-a-quantum-fluid</link><description>玻色-爱因斯坦凝聚体（BEC）通常被描述为“物质的第五态”：一种量子态，在这种状态下，许多粒子失去了各自的身份，并表现为一个集体物体。 60 多年来，研究人员一直试图从激子（电子空穴对）中产生这种凝聚体，作为实现宏观量子相干性的固态途径，这对量子技术很有用。这在可控半导体器件中很难实现，因为光学产生的激子的寿命非常短，约为十亿分之一秒，而且BEC通常是用真空中的超冷气体来实现的。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/scientists-reveal-hidden-structure-of-a-quantum-fluid2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 23:39:02 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/scientists-reveal-hidden-structure-of-a-quantum-fluid</guid></item><item><title>临床医生在人工智能时代浏览可穿戴数据的框架</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/a-framework-for-clinicians-navigating-wearable-data-in-the-ai-era</link><description>本视角概述了临床医生从可穿戴设备中导航生理数据的框架，称为“ &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/a-framework-for-clinicians-navigating-wearable-data-in-the-ai-era2.png" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 23:24:02 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/a-framework-for-clinicians-navigating-wearable-data-in-the-ai-era</guid></item><item><title>磁性掺杂剂帮助量子点利用光进行化学反应</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/magnetic-dopants-help-quantum-dots-use-light-for-chemical-reactions</link><description>洛斯阿拉莫斯国家实验室的科学家们展示了一种新的量子点机制，可以显着扩大光驱动化学的范围。通过将磁性锰掺杂剂引入半导体量子点，该团队创建了一种超快自旋交换途径，可以在热电子能量以热量形式损失之前捕获热电子能量，并用它来驱动化学还原。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/magnetic-dopants-help-quantum-dots-use-light-for-chemical-reactions.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 23:09:02 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/magnetic-dopants-help-quantum-dots-use-light-for-chemical-reactions</guid></item></channel></rss>